WEBVTT

1
01:01:41.602 --> 01:01:49.602
I sit in the presence of the Most High. Hallelujah.

2
01:01:52.602 --> 01:01:58.602
December 25. Last Sunday of the year.

3
01:01:59.602 --> 01:02:05.602
If I am grateful for something, one of the things, I am grateful for many things.

4
01:02:06.602 --> 01:02:10.602
But I am also grateful for the theme we have addressed this year.

5
01:02:10.602 --> 01:02:12.602
Here I am, Lord, send me.

6
01:02:13.602 --> 01:02:17.602
I will read you the Bible verse, I will read you the chapter one more time.

7
01:02:17.602 --> 01:02:21.602
And I can still remember well, that first Sunday of the year,

8
01:02:21.602 --> 01:02:25.602
when I read it for the first time to introduce the theme.

9
01:02:25.602 --> 01:02:27.602
The year went by so fast, people. It's just not normal, is it?

10
01:02:29.602 --> 01:02:30.602
It went fast, didn't it?

11
01:02:32.602 --> 01:02:33.602
Suddenly it was gone again.

12
01:02:34.602 --> 01:02:37.602
This year we had a wonderful youth camp.

13
01:02:37.602 --> 01:02:39.602
All youth, let yourselves be heard.

14
01:02:40.602 --> 01:02:41.602
Okay, three youth then.

15
01:02:43.602 --> 01:02:50.602
It was amazing. It was such a nice year as far as a year without covid goes. Amen.

16
01:02:51.602 --> 01:02:52.602
Amen, right?

17
01:02:53.602 --> 01:02:56.602
I have had a runny nose the past two weeks, quite a bit.

18
01:02:56.602 --> 01:02:59.602
I even lay in bed. But we are back on stage.

19
01:03:01.602 --> 01:03:05.602
And covid is gone, in Jesus' name. No more lockdowns, amen.

20
01:03:06.602 --> 01:03:08.602
Amen. No more face masks, wonderful.

21
01:03:11.602 --> 01:03:18.602
But I can still remember well that I was reading Isaiah High Success for the first time.

22
01:03:20.602 --> 01:03:27.602
And for me, I don't know, I find every year amazing and I find every theme amazing.

23
01:03:27.602 --> 01:03:35.602
Because in prayer I experience every time that God brings me somewhere as a church family.

24
01:03:35.602 --> 01:03:38.602
But this year I had a very special deep feeling about it.

25
01:03:39.602 --> 01:03:43.602
Sometimes you can't quite put it into words, but I found it a wonderful theme.

26
01:03:44.602 --> 01:03:54.602
As I read through Isaiah 6, I read that Isaiah 6 is filled with the glory of God.

27
01:03:55.602 --> 01:04:04.602
And I am grateful for Open Church that we are dedicating ourselves to experiencing more of that glory of God.

28
01:04:04.602 --> 01:04:06.602
However that may look.

29
01:04:06.602 --> 01:04:11.602
And I am thankful to Vanessa for leading in praise and worship.

30
01:04:11.602 --> 01:04:16.602
And that we as a church are in prayer and that we are fasting and that we are learning.

31
01:04:16.602 --> 01:04:19.602
And for some people, that is a journey to learn to pray.

32
01:04:20.602 --> 01:04:25.602
Some people enjoy singing together, some people enjoy sitting in the Word.

33
01:04:25.602 --> 01:04:29.602
But you know that Jesus says, my house shall be a house of prayer.

34
01:04:30.602 --> 01:04:37.602
And what I read in Isaiah 6 is that Isaiah is taken to the glory of God.

35
01:04:37.602 --> 01:04:41.602
And he gets to see a picture of how great God is.

36
01:04:42.602 --> 01:04:44.602
We have a great God, people.

37
01:04:45.602 --> 01:04:46.602
We do not have a theoretical God.

38
01:04:47.602 --> 01:04:48.602
We do not have a philosophical God.

39
01:04:49.602 --> 01:04:53.602
We do not have a God who says, if you behave this way, you will have an okay life.

40
01:04:54.602 --> 01:04:57.602
We do not have a behaviorist God.

41
01:04:58.602 --> 01:05:03.602
A book where people have invented all sorts of rules and you have to do it this way.

42
01:05:03.602 --> 01:05:06.602
And if you do it this way, then you are the best you.

43
01:05:06.602 --> 01:05:08.602
That is not the God of Christianity.

44
01:05:08.602 --> 01:05:12.602
The God of Christianity is He who fills the temple with smoke. Amen.

45
01:05:13.602 --> 01:05:17.602
And this is what I read in Isaiah 6. He is almighty, people.

46
01:05:18.602 --> 01:05:20.602
He is the God of the heavenly armies.

47
01:05:20.602 --> 01:05:27.602
He is so wonderful and He is so great that when Isaiah comes into eye contact with God,

48
01:05:27.602 --> 01:05:34.602
he falls down as dead because he understands that he is just a man who is so imperfect,

49
01:05:34.602 --> 01:05:37.602
while he stands face to face with He who is perfect.

50
01:05:37.602 --> 01:05:40.602
His name is, by the way, Jesus.

51
01:05:41.602 --> 01:05:44.602
I am going to read something to you. Chapter 6.

52
01:05:45.602 --> 01:05:47.602
In case you have never heard it before.

53
01:05:48.602 --> 01:05:49.602
Isaiah Chapter 6.

54
01:05:49.602 --> 01:05:54.602
In the year that King Uzziah died, I saw the Lord.

55
01:05:55.602 --> 01:06:01.602
I bless us in the name of Jesus that as we enter 2023, we will see the Lord.

56
01:06:02.602 --> 01:06:06.602
I pray in Jesus' name that you will not only behold the church.

57
01:06:06.602 --> 01:06:08.602
I pray that you will not only see the works of the church.

58
01:06:08.602 --> 01:06:12.602
I pray that you will not only see open winter kitchens.

59
01:06:12.602 --> 01:06:13.602
Oh, that's cool.

60
01:06:13.602 --> 01:06:18.602
I pray that you will not only come to church because there is a good vibe.

61
01:06:18.602 --> 01:06:23.602
In other words, I pray that you do not come to the church and that you only see the church.

62
01:06:23.602 --> 01:06:28.602
I pray that you see the head of the church, the person around whom the church revolves,

63
01:06:28.602 --> 01:06:31.602
that you will see him face to face in Jesus' name.

64
01:06:31.602 --> 01:06:33.602
That is what it is all about.

65
01:06:34.602 --> 01:06:42.602
Oh, I earnestly pray that Christians will not be blind to the person around whom it truly revolves.

66
01:06:43.602 --> 01:06:44.602
How terrible would that be?

67
01:06:44.602 --> 01:06:45.602
How terrible would that be?

68
01:06:45.602 --> 01:06:49.602
That you would come to the church your whole life, that you would participate in teams,

69
01:06:49.602 --> 01:06:53.602
that you would even put money in the collection plate, that you might stand on the stage,

70
01:06:53.602 --> 01:06:55.602
that you would be involved in one of the teams,

71
01:06:55.602 --> 01:06:59.602
but that your whole life long, because of religion and obstacles,

72
01:06:59.602 --> 01:07:03.602
you would miss the person with the big P around whom it truly revolves.

73
01:07:03.602 --> 01:07:05.602
This would be horrible.

74
01:07:06.602 --> 01:07:10.602
My prayer as a church is that we will behold him for who he truly is.

75
01:07:10.602 --> 01:07:11.602
Amen.

76
01:07:12.602 --> 01:07:13.602
I will continue.

77
01:07:14.602 --> 01:07:17.602
In the year that King Uzziah died, I saw the Lord.

78
01:07:17.602 --> 01:07:20.602
He was sitting on a high and exalted throne.

79
01:07:20.602 --> 01:07:24.602
The hem of his robe filled the whole temple.

80
01:07:24.602 --> 01:07:28.602
There were angels above him. Each angel had six wings.

81
01:07:28.602 --> 01:07:31.602
With two wings the angels covered their face.

82
01:07:31.602 --> 01:07:33.602
With two wings they covered their feet.

83
01:07:33.602 --> 01:07:36.602
And with two wings they flew.

84
01:07:36.602 --> 01:07:38.602
And the angels called to one another,

85
01:07:38.602 --> 01:07:42.602
Holy, holy, holy is the Lord of hosts.

86
01:07:43.602 --> 01:07:48.602
The earth is full of his glorious power and majesty.

87
01:07:48.602 --> 01:07:54.602
Church, I repeat, the earth is full of his glorious power and majesty.

88
01:07:54.602 --> 01:07:56.602
We are not waiting for a heaven.

89
01:07:56.602 --> 01:07:59.602
We are not waiting for a better afterlife.

90
01:07:59.602 --> 01:08:05.602
This earth is full of his glorious power and majesty.

91
01:08:05.602 --> 01:08:08.602
The here and now is filled with Jesus.

92
01:08:08.602 --> 01:08:11.602
It is our task as a church to show you

93
01:08:11.602 --> 01:08:15.602
how wonderful it is to have a life together with Jesus.

94
01:08:15.602 --> 01:08:18.602
For if you are going to see Jesus now,

95
01:08:18.602 --> 01:08:21.602
Isaiah does not say when he has a vision of God,

96
01:08:21.602 --> 01:08:23.602
it is wonderful in heaven.

97
01:08:23.602 --> 01:08:29.602
Isaiah says that the angels cry, the earth is filled with his majesty.

98
01:08:29.602 --> 01:08:34.602
And living with God is seeing how wonderful life is. Amen?

99
01:08:34.602 --> 01:08:36.602
Amen.

100
01:08:39.602 --> 01:08:41.602
Verse 4.

101
01:08:41.602 --> 01:08:45.602
They cried out so loudly that the doorposts of the temple shook.

102
01:08:45.602 --> 01:08:49.602
Also, the temple was filled with smoke.

103
01:08:49.602 --> 01:08:51.602
And then I cried out, help, I am going to die,

104
01:08:51.602 --> 01:08:54.602
for I am a man from whom no good word comes.

105
01:08:54.602 --> 01:08:58.602
And I belong to a people from whom no good word comes.

106
01:08:58.602 --> 01:09:02.602
And now I have seen the king, the Lord of heavenly hosts.

107
01:09:02.602 --> 01:09:04.602
There must have been a vision.

108
01:09:04.602 --> 01:09:06.602
But one of the angels flew to me.

109
01:09:06.602 --> 01:09:09.602
He had in his hand a tongs with a piece of glowing coal

110
01:09:09.602 --> 01:09:11.602
that he had taken from the altar.

111
01:09:11.602 --> 01:09:14.602
He touched my mouth with the glowing coal.

112
01:09:14.602 --> 01:09:18.602
Then he said, pay attention, this coal has touched your mouth.

113
01:09:18.602 --> 01:09:20.602
Now your mouth and your heart are cleansed.

114
01:09:20.602 --> 01:09:25.602
Everything in which you have been disobedient to God has been removed and forgiven.

115
01:09:25.602 --> 01:09:27.602
This was not Jesus.

116
01:09:27.602 --> 01:09:33.602
This was an angel who did something there with Isaiah.

117
01:09:33.602 --> 01:09:39.602
I know someone who has done something for everyone instead of for one person.

118
01:09:39.602 --> 01:09:42.602
I know someone who did not take coal from the fire.

119
01:09:42.602 --> 01:09:44.602
I know someone who is the fire itself.

120
01:09:44.602 --> 01:09:49.602
I know someone who has not done something for one person for one lifetime.

121
01:09:49.602 --> 01:09:52.602
I know someone who has done something for all of humanity.

122
01:09:52.602 --> 01:09:55.602
His name is Jesus and let's give him a round of applause.

123
01:09:59.602 --> 01:10:01.602
Glorious, the name of Jesus.

124
01:10:04.602 --> 01:10:07.602
Then I heard the Lord say, whom shall I send?

125
01:10:07.602 --> 01:10:09.602
Who will go for us?

126
01:10:09.602 --> 01:10:13.602
And I answered, here I am Lord, send me the theme of this year.

127
01:10:13.602 --> 01:10:18.602
And then He said, go and say to this people, listen but do not understand.

128
01:10:18.602 --> 01:10:21.602
Look but do not let it penetrate you.

129
01:10:21.602 --> 01:10:23.602
Make the heart of this people stubborn.

130
01:10:23.602 --> 01:10:26.602
Make their ears deaf and seal their eyes shut.

131
01:10:26.602 --> 01:10:31.602
Then they will see nothing with their eyes and hear nothing with their ears and understand nothing with their heart.

132
01:10:31.602 --> 01:10:35.602
Therefore they will not return to me and I will not heal them.

133
01:10:35.602 --> 01:10:40.602
And I asked Him and I asked Lord, how long will this last?

134
01:10:40.602 --> 01:10:45.602
And He answered, until the cities are destroyed and there are no inhabitants left.

135
01:10:45.602 --> 01:10:49.602
Until all the houses are broken down and no one lives in them.

136
01:10:49.602 --> 01:10:51.602
Until the whole land is devastated.

137
01:10:51.602 --> 01:10:57.602
For I will drive the people far away and the land will be almost completely uninhabited.

138
01:10:57.602 --> 01:11:02.602
But a tenth of the whole people will remain there and the land will be devastated again.

139
01:11:02.602 --> 01:11:09.602
But the people will be like an oak that has been chopped down and of which only the stump remains.

140
01:11:09.602 --> 01:11:12.602
In that stump is still strength.

141
01:11:12.602 --> 01:11:16.602
Therefore, there will be new life. Say new life.

142
01:11:16.602 --> 01:11:20.602
That is really amazing, say new life. That is really such a church thing, say new life.

143
01:11:20.602 --> 01:11:23.602
Therefore, new life will grow out of the church.

144
01:11:23.602 --> 01:11:29.602
Thus, new life will also arise from the remnant of the people.

145
01:11:29.602 --> 01:11:31.602
This is the church of Jesus Christ.

146
01:11:31.602 --> 01:11:34.602
For the remnant belongs to the Lord.

147
01:11:34.602 --> 01:11:36.602
You belong to the Lord.

148
01:11:36.602 --> 01:11:39.602
The only thing you have to do is believe in Him.

149
01:11:39.602 --> 01:11:43.602
For here it is written, it is indeed a holy sap.

150
01:11:43.602 --> 01:11:45.602
Hallelujah.

151
01:11:45.602 --> 01:11:47.602
Hallelujah.

152
01:11:50.602 --> 01:11:52.602
This is Isaiah High Success.

153
01:11:53.602 --> 01:11:57.602
I have unpleasant news, to be very honest.

154
01:11:57.602 --> 01:11:59.602
Isaiah is setting out.

155
01:11:59.602 --> 01:12:02.602
He is going to do what he must do at the command of the Lord.

156
01:12:02.602 --> 01:12:05.602
And he is doing his best. He lives his life for God.

157
01:12:05.602 --> 01:12:07.602
He is going for it.

158
01:12:07.602 --> 01:12:11.602
By the way, he admits that he is also a man from whom no good word comes.

159
01:12:11.602 --> 01:12:15.602
So he admits that he is also a broken man, just like you and me.

160
01:12:15.602 --> 01:12:19.602
The church is filled with people, just like you and me and Isaiah.

161
01:12:20.602 --> 01:12:22.602
But Isaiah is obedient to God.

162
01:12:22.602 --> 01:12:24.602
And Isaiah does what God tells him.

163
01:12:24.602 --> 01:12:28.602
Who shall I send? Here I am. Send me.

164
01:12:28.602 --> 01:12:30.602
Isaiah goes out.

165
01:12:30.602 --> 01:12:35.602
And he indeed proclaims the Word of God to a sinful people.

166
01:12:35.602 --> 01:12:38.602
He indeed goes to a dark world.

167
01:12:38.602 --> 01:12:42.602
And it certainly has an effect of what Isaiah has done.

168
01:12:42.602 --> 01:12:45.602
He is one of the greats among the prophets.

169
01:12:45.602 --> 01:12:48.602
But the bad news that actually needs to be told.

170
01:12:48.602 --> 01:12:52.602
Is that after Isaiah the whole world is not saved.

171
01:12:52.602 --> 01:12:56.602
Isaiah had no lasting effect.

172
01:12:56.602 --> 01:13:00.602
What Isaiah did was nice for a short time.

173
01:13:00.602 --> 01:13:04.602
There is another prophet I sometimes think of.

174
01:13:04.602 --> 01:13:07.602
His name is Jonah.

175
01:13:07.602 --> 01:13:09.602
Jonah goes out.

176
01:13:09.602 --> 01:13:11.602
Receives a command from the Lord.

177
01:13:11.602 --> 01:13:13.602
Just like Isaiah.

178
01:13:13.602 --> 01:13:17.602
Instead of Isaiah who says here I am Lord send me.

179
01:13:17.602 --> 01:13:21.602
Jonah has a slightly different reaction.

180
01:13:21.602 --> 01:13:24.602
He says here I am not Lord do not send me.

181
01:13:27.602 --> 01:13:30.602
Most people know the story of Jonah.

182
01:13:30.602 --> 01:13:32.602
Jonah flees.

183
01:13:32.602 --> 01:13:34.602
In the end, God catches him.

184
01:13:34.602 --> 01:13:36.602
Thank you, Lord, that your hand is so far-reaching.

185
01:13:36.602 --> 01:13:39.602
That you can even grasp stubborn people like me.

186
01:13:39.602 --> 01:13:40.602
With your love.

187
01:13:40.602 --> 01:13:41.602
With your command.

188
01:13:41.602 --> 01:13:44.602
With your calling that you have for people.

189
01:13:45.602 --> 01:13:49.602
Wonderful that I was like a Jonah but that you saved me.

190
01:13:49.602 --> 01:13:51.602
Jonah goes out.

191
01:13:51.602 --> 01:13:53.602
But here is the story.

192
01:13:53.602 --> 01:13:57.602
Jonah goes out with a warning for the city of Nineveh.

193
01:13:57.602 --> 01:13:59.602
You all know the story.

194
01:13:59.602 --> 01:14:02.602
He goes out to Nineveh and he saves Nineveh.

195
01:14:02.602 --> 01:14:04.602
We all think together.

196
01:14:04.602 --> 01:14:07.602
Wow, luckily Nineveh is saved.

197
01:14:07.602 --> 01:14:09.602
I have bad news for you.

198
01:14:09.602 --> 01:14:12.602
Shortly after, Nineveh fell anyway.

199
01:14:13.602 --> 01:14:17.602
So Nineveh in the time of Jonah was saved.

200
01:14:17.602 --> 01:14:20.602
Jonah goes to the center of Nineveh.

201
01:14:20.602 --> 01:14:22.602
Jumps on a stage.

202
01:14:22.602 --> 01:14:25.602
Calls out about judgment and unrighteousness.

203
01:14:25.602 --> 01:14:27.602
And what happens when you do so without.

204
01:14:27.602 --> 01:14:29.602
Nineveh comes to repentance.

205
01:14:29.602 --> 01:14:31.602
Everyone thinks all's well that ends well.

206
01:14:31.602 --> 01:14:33.602
Nice to listen to a person.

207
01:14:33.602 --> 01:14:35.602
If you behave like that, then it will be good again.

208
01:14:35.602 --> 01:14:38.602
Unfortunately, great powers came afterwards.

209
01:14:38.602 --> 01:14:40.602
Nineveh has still fallen.

210
01:14:40.602 --> 01:14:43.602
Nineveh fell back into its own sin.

211
01:14:43.602 --> 01:14:47.602
Nineveh has ultimately been lost in their own sin.

212
01:14:47.602 --> 01:14:50.602
And from sin ultimately comes judgment.

213
01:14:50.602 --> 01:14:52.602
I have no other message.

214
01:14:52.602 --> 01:14:54.602
From sin comes judgment.

215
01:14:54.602 --> 01:14:55.602
From judgment comes death.

216
01:14:55.602 --> 01:14:57.602
There is no other message.

217
01:15:00.602 --> 01:15:03.602
When I am listening to the wonderful things.

218
01:15:03.602 --> 01:15:05.602
I did it with premeditation.

219
01:15:05.602 --> 01:15:07.602
When I am listening to all the wonderful things.

220
01:15:07.602 --> 01:15:09.602
That people are naming.

221
01:15:09.602 --> 01:15:11.602
When I say go ahead and stand up.

222
01:15:11.602 --> 01:15:14.602
And just say something you are thankful for.

223
01:15:14.602 --> 01:15:17.602
All the things we speak can be things to be thankful for.

224
01:15:17.602 --> 01:15:19.602
But let me show you a few things.

225
01:15:19.602 --> 01:15:22.602
About what we have done as a church.

226
01:15:22.602 --> 01:15:24.602
So this year in Open Church.

227
01:15:24.602 --> 01:15:28.602
We have set up an open winter kitchen.

228
01:15:28.602 --> 01:15:32.602
We have provided people with free meals.

229
01:15:32.602 --> 01:15:34.602
And we will continue until April.

230
01:15:34.602 --> 01:15:35.602
Why?

231
01:15:35.602 --> 01:15:38.602
Because it is wonderful to have friendship together.

232
01:15:38.602 --> 01:15:41.602
It is great to be able to feed people together.

233
01:15:41.602 --> 01:15:45.602
One person needs it from a financial aspect.

234
01:15:45.602 --> 01:15:47.602
The other person needs it to.

235
01:15:47.602 --> 01:15:48.602
Maybe they are lonely.

236
01:15:48.602 --> 01:15:49.602
Maybe you are divorced.

237
01:15:49.602 --> 01:15:51.602
And you thought to yourself, what am I going to do now?

238
01:15:51.602 --> 01:15:53.602
And then you go to the church.

239
01:15:53.602 --> 01:15:55.602
And there are wonderful people who come together.

240
01:15:55.602 --> 01:15:57.602
Then you can enjoy eating together.

241
01:15:57.602 --> 01:15:58.602
Maybe you are filthy rich.

242
01:15:58.602 --> 01:15:59.602
And you think to yourself.

243
01:15:59.602 --> 01:16:01.602
It's also fun to be a part of that.

244
01:16:01.602 --> 01:16:03.602
And then we all go eat there together.

245
01:16:03.602 --> 01:16:05.602
Can I contribute something as well?

246
01:16:05.602 --> 01:16:07.602
And then we have a good time on Tuesday.

247
01:16:07.602 --> 01:16:09.602
Tuesday is just an amazing time.

248
01:16:09.602 --> 01:16:10.602
